diff --git a/docs/model-provider-routes.md b/docs/model-provider-routes.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..9e893a38f1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/model-provider-routes.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Model provider routes
+
+Use an exact model-to-provider mapping to select models from different providers
+in the ordinary model picker. Models without an entry use the session's default
+provider.
+
+```toml
+model = "gpt-6.1-sol"
+model_catalog_json = "/absolute/path/to/models.json"
+
+[model_provider_routes]
+auto = "ai-mux"
+
+[model_providers.ai-mux]
+name = "ai-mux"
+base_url = "http://127.0.0.1:8090/v1"
+wire_api = "responses"
+requires_openai_auth = false
+supports_websockets = false
+```
+
+The custom model catalog must include a visible entry with slug `auto` and the
+capabilities of that route. This mapping does not rewrite the model ID sent to
+the provider. Provider definitions and routes must be in trusted user, system,
+managed, or runtime configuration; project-local routes are ignored. A route
+cannot select a different provider when managed policy requires one.
+
+Changing providers creates fresh transport state. Authentication is resolved
+using the selected provider; cached WebSockets and provider-specific response
+headers are not copied between endpoints. Startup prewarming is disabled while
+model routes are configured because the next selected model may use another
+provider.
+
+Restart Codex after changing the model catalog or installing a build with this
+feature. Existing processes and app-server daemons continue using their loaded
+binary and catalog.
+
+## Routed model and reasoning display
+
+For configured model routes, the Responses `openai-model` header or equivalent
+stream metadata reports the concrete backend model. Codex treats that as expected
+provider routing, emits a `ProviderRouting` model-reroute notification, and shows
+`selected alias → routed model` in the terminal footer. The selected alias remains
+unchanged for later requests. The route label resets at the start of each turn so
+an old backend is not presented as the current choice before metadata arrives.
+
+Reasoning summaries from mapped models appear in the live status details and stay
+visible in the conversation after completion, including summaries without a bold
+heading. No reasoning is synthesized when an upstream omits it. Buffered upstreams
+can only expose their reasoning when their response reaches the router.
